    "body": "Follow-up to #4307, which documented the `typescript.tsdk` workaround for Nix.\r\n\r\nThis PR covers two remaining gaps:\r\n- Document that `typescript.tsdk` only works with TypeScript <= 6.x, since TS 7 removed `tsserverlibrary.js` from the npm package.\r\n- Add a runtime-lookup example for globally installed TypeScript: try `util.get_typescript_server_path()` first, then fall back to `npm root -g` (with equivalent commands for pnpm/yarn included in the comments).",
